### What new functionality are you requesting?

A new resource, `aws_datazone_project_profile`, to manage Amazon DataZone / SageMaker Unified Studio project profiles.

**This is not `aws_datazone_environment_profile`.** Environment profiles are a DataZone V1 concept and already exist in the provider. Project profiles are the V2 / SageMaker Unified Studio object, backed by a different API (`CreateProjectProfile`) and a different CloudFormation type (`AWS::DataZone::ProjectProfile`)

### Description

A project profile is the template every SageMaker Unified Studio project is created from. It declares which blueprints (capabilities) a project gets, **in which deployment mode**, with which parameter overrides, and which AWS account and region the resulting projects land in. It is the central object of a Unified Studio deployment — the domain is the container, the blueprints are the inventory, and the project profile is the thing an end user actually consumes.

There is no equivalent in the `aws` provider. A complete Unified Studio deployment is currently impossible without `awscc`.

### Potential Terraform Configuration

### Minimal usage

Blueprint IDs resolve through the existing `aws_datazone_environment_blueprint` data source, so no new lookup mechanism is needed:

```terraform
data "aws_caller_identity" "current" {}
data "aws_region" "current" {}

data "aws_datazone_environment_blueprint" "tooling" {
  domain_id = aws_datazone_domain.example.id
  name      = "Tooling"
  managed   = true
}

resource "aws_datazone_project_profile" "example" {
  domain_identifier      = aws_datazone_domain.example.id
  domain_unit_identifier = aws_datazone_domain.example.root_domain_unit_id
  name                   = "research"
  description            = "Research project profile"
  status                 = "ENABLED"

  environment_configurations {
    name                     = "Tooling"
    environment_blueprint_id = data.aws_datazone_environment_blueprint.tooling.id
    deployment_mode          = "ON_CREATE"
    deployment_order         = 0

    aws_account {
      aws_account_id = data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id
    }

    aws_region {
      region_name = data.aws_region.current.name
    }
  }
}
```

### The pattern this resource is needed for: on-demand capabilities with a pinned cost ceiling

```terraform
locals {
  blueprints = ["Tooling", "RedshiftServerless", "MLExperiments"]
}

data "aws_datazone_environment_blueprint" "this" {
  for_each  = toset(local.blueprints)
  domain_id = aws_datazone_domain.example.id
  name      = each.key
  managed   = true
}

resource "aws_datazone_project_profile" "research" {
  domain_identifier      = aws_datazone_domain.example.id
  domain_unit_identifier = aws_datazone_domain_unit.research.id
  name                   = "research"
  status                 = "ENABLED"

  # Mandatory floor: provisioned with every project
  environment_configurations {
    name                     = "Tooling"
    environment_blueprint_id = data.aws_datazone_environment_blueprint.tooling.id
    deployment_mode          = "ON_CREATE"
    deployment_order         = 0

    aws_account { aws_account_id = data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id }
    aws_region { region_name = data.aws_region.current.name }
  }

  # Offered but not provisioned until a user asks, with the cost ceiling pinned
  environment_configurations {
    name                     = "RedshiftServerless"
    environment_blueprint_id = data.aws_datazone_environment_blueprint.redshift.id
    deployment_mode          = "ON_DEMAND"

    aws_account { aws_account_id = data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id }
    aws_region { region_name = data.aws_region.current.name }

    configuration_parameters {
      parameter_overrides {
        name        = "redshiftBaseCapacity"
        value       = "8"
        is_editable = false
      }
    }
  }

  environment_configurations {
    name                     = "MLExperiments"
    environment_blueprint_id = data.aws_datazone_environment_blueprint.ml_experiments.id
    deployment_mode          = "ON_DEMAND"

    aws_account { aws_account_id = data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id }
    aws_region { region_name = data.aws_region.current.name }
  }
}
```

Note that `deployment_order` is set only on `ON_CREATE` entries — on-demand capabilities have no project creation to be ordered within.


### References

- API: `CreateProjectProfile`, `GetProjectProfile`, `UpdateProjectProfile`, `DeleteProjectProfile`, `ListProjectProfiles`
  https://docs.aws.amazon.com/datazone/latest/APIReference/API_CreateProjectProfile.html
- CloudFormation: `AWS::DataZone::ProjectProfile`
  https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/aws-resource-datazone-projectprofile.html
- Prior art: `awscc_datazone_project_profile`
  https://registry.terraform.io/providers/hashicorp/awscc/latest/docs/resources/datazone_project_profile
- SageMaker Unified Studio project profiles and deployment modes
  https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker-unified-studio/latest/adminguide/project-profiles.html
- Related, already tracked:
  - #50106 — `aws_datazone_domain_unit` (a project profile's `domain_unit_identifier` needs it)
  - #40891 — `aws_datazone_group_profile` (groups must be registered before they can be granted use of a profile)
  - #45198 — `aws_datazone_project` missing V2 arguments (a project is created *from* a project profile)

### Would you like to implement the enhancement?

No

